Rejig: what the MCP companion needs from the editor. Applies to ios_homescreen/api.py,
ui/session.py, ui/app.py and ui/static/js/actions.js from
https://github.com/YakupEmreYerli/ios-homescreen at commit
97649547dbc44295e451c6bf130a87404481e10c. The companion and the editor page share one editor
session, and the page reloads the session's state only after its own jobs. Without a check, a
draft the page planned before an MCP read and apply could overwrite that newer layout with no
warning. /api/apply and /api/backups/restore now take an optional expect_read (the read file
the plan was made against) and answer read_changed when the session has read the phone since;
the page sends the read its draft is based on. A restore given expect_read also refuses, like
apply, when the phone itself changed since that read, and one given expect_digest refuses
(backup_changed) when the backup no longer holds what was approved. /api/state also names the
folders this run keeps reads and backups in, which demo mode puts in a scratch folder.
